# Defaults for running the CI workflows locally with nektos/act.
#
#   act -j architecture      # one job
#   act push                 # everything the push event triggers
#
# Two things act cannot do, so a green local run is necessary but not sufficient:
#
#   - It only runs Linux containers. The macos-latest and windows-latest legs of
#     the test matrix are skipped, and those are the reason the matrix exists —
#     the scaffolder branches on runtime.GOOS in interpreter discovery, venv
#     paths, start scripts and the --install target.
#   - The runner image is not GitHub's. catthehacker/ubuntu is close, but a
#     failure that depends on preinstalled tooling can differ.
#
# The image is pinned to the medium variant: act-latest is ~1GB and carries a
# full toolchain we do not need, since setup-go installs Go itself.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04

# Match the host so Apple Silicon runs natively instead of emulating amd64,
# which is several times slower.
--container-architecture linux/arm64

# Run one job at a time.
#
# act shares a single host directory across every job it runs, where real GitHub
# Actions gives each job its own checkout on its own runner. Run concurrently,
# the architecture job regenerates golden files while the test job is reading
# them, and the test job fails for a reason that cannot happen on GitHub.
--concurrent-jobs 1
